          ":question/id": "681d8619-9082-56b4-9422-241cad7644a3",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-326016",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/0f/0f9ee37fe5f1cf32ba470b24e5d27b4164bd00a0caeae0536ae48d4cc5836c6d.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "![](images/c9/c95e718a0c30e2be1f3678123eea0006b17fd781305c06a4f277488c2389337f.png)\n\nIn $△OXT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OX=\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot |\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OX}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OX}=-\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $XT=2|\\mathbf{b}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{XT}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-2\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{t}=\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{t}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+\\mu \\mathbf{b}=-\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{b}∦\\mathbf{a},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{7}{4}$ and $\\mu =-2$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186403878,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/choices": [
