          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/hard"
          },
          ":question/id": "1d7e3219-6ed4-5e79-b442-f16e9eeecf24",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/b6/b6e5e69988b962627f39af49e25a904769a7de6bbebf8193e19d1540895ef992.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "![](images/6b/6be1c7aa854a75ea143bc6b0b70317128d3f83f7868db4eb1ad50b326d223b8c.png)\n\nIn $△OMR$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OM=\\frac{1}{4}|\\mathbf{q}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OM}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{q}.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $MR=\\frac{4}{3}|\\mathbf{p}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{MR}$ has the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{p}$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{MR}=-\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{p}.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r} & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MR} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{q}-\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{p} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{p}+\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{q}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{r}=\\lambda \\mathbf{p}+\\mu \\mathbf{q}=-\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{p}+\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{q}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{p}∦\\mathbf{q},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{4}{3}$ and $\\mu =\\frac{1}{4}$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186514764,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/choices": [
                {
                  ":answer/id": "e30b8b0a-5c41-508a-800a-779854ec5eb2",
                  ":answer/type": {
                    ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                  },
                  ":answer/value": "\\frac{5}{3}",
                  ":db/id": 17592186514787
                }
              ],
              ":answer-field/correct": {
                ":answer/id": "e30b8b0a-5c41-508a-800a-779854ec5eb2",
