          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"
          },
          ":question/id": "d46199db-7d10-55ea-8f4c-bb6ccaaae660",
          ":question/problem": "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram on a square grid](images/c6/c6bc3baa512da1ef4f9fffc94d0f1069402f58828a9b8ff732a6b97b1543597e.png)\n\nThe dashed route goes from $O$ to $A$ to $C$. Use the grid to compare each part with $\\mathbf{a}$ or $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "![Completed vector path](images/5d/5d7bbadbc141798871c16c1175696cf27628e2966c84d2bb2f744ff65d527c71.png)\n\nFollow the supplied route $O\\to A\\to C$. On the grid, $OA$ is twice the length of $\\mathbf{a}$ and points in the same direction, so $\\overrightarrow{OA}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nThe segment from $A$ to $C$ moves six squares right and three squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves two squares right and one square down. Thus $AC=3|\\mathbf{b}|$, with the same direction, and $\\overrightarrow{AC}=3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AC}\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=2$ and $\\mu=3$."
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186735013,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/choices": [
                {
                  ":answer/id": "83aa297f-c7f9-5297-b7ee-0b257f47927b",
                  ":answer/type": {
                    ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                  },
                  ":answer/value": "2",
                  ":db/id": 17592186735004
                }
              ],
              ":answer-field/correct": {
                ":answer/id": "83aa297f-c7f9-5297-b7ee-0b257f47927b",
