          ":question/id": "7a8a858b-29c0-589f-be68-44f29738bc0d",
          ":question/problem": "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/7e/7eea4d14d23ec6a08512837065a0e8c314fddde9eb01d8eac638d4c5e5e9e00f.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "![Completed vector route](images/45/458c5b35ce2448591cee94390f436cc0c835c14f79e1cab2c55e960cab1b6fed.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $6$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares up. Thus $OX=3|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-3\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $3$ squares left and $6$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares left and $4$ squares up. Thus $XC=\\frac{3}{2}|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-3\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-3$ and $\\mu=\\frac{3}{2}$."
        },
