          ":question/id": "bc8e6b34-f02b-5448-931c-94334c21f73e",
          ":question/problem": "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/9a/9adcf4f0295b807efed07a34d2bff2eee01a5229fd367f026fed6de705c34199.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "![Completed vector route](images/2c/2cf0ee7b5174b6d89944b5e3d6a48086048362ad029235a7ded707f735f4b722.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $10$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $4$ squares up. Thus $OX=\\frac{5}{2}|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $1$ square right and $1$ square down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square up. Thus $XC=1|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\mu=-1$."
        },
