          ":question/id": "eb17691f-ad45-50d8-9bf1-066fefc0ee32",
          ":question/problem": "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/43/43d8df5853adab4bc9f7ae8138675c855dec0281cb0cd9b053539a116f8b20d5.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "![Completed vector route](images/5a/5a64645ccdb41247aafd9b4ffb99718662e93aae73ae498428e2ceadda8e2c54.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $5$ squares right and $10$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares right and $4$ squares up. Thus $OX=\\frac{5}{2}|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $6$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares up. Thus $XC=3|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-3\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}-3\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=-3\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-3$ and $\\mu=\\frac{5}{2}$."
        },
