          },
          ":question/id": "eee74ea9-5018-5a1b-8460-e61ca7767d79",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-120285",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/c4/c4d26b3db6446f586ca47634d9f9a3a004968a0081b8859ce46b4b4af799d066.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=\\mathbf{h},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OI}=\\mathbf{i}$ and $J$ divides $\\overline{HI}$ in the ratio $HJ:JI=3:7.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=\\mathbf{h},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OHI,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HI} & =\\overset{\\to }{HO}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{h}+\\mathbf{i} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $HJ:JI=3:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{HJ}=\\frac{3}{10}\\overset{\\to }{HI}=\\frac{3}{10}(\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{h}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{3}{10}(\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{h}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{3}{10}\\mathbf{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186256383,
