          ":question/id": "e34b700c-a9ab-5795-931b-c570187a69f9",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-120294",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/70/707beca1d856414e25874cc0b56c6654fbb41d699f01106b6749d49408b39aee.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=\\mathbf{u},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\mathbf{v}$ and $W$ divides $\\overline{UV}$ in the ratio $UW:WV=7:2.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OW}.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=\\mathbf{u},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{UW}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OUV,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =\\overset{\\to }{UO}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{v}-\\mathbf{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $UW:WV=7:2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{UW}=\\frac{7}{9}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=\\frac{7}{9}(\\mathbf{v}-\\mathbf{u}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OW} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{7}{9}(\\mathbf{v}-\\mathbf{u}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{7}{9}\\mathbf{v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
