          ":question/id": "1d6d86cb-c355-5347-a86b-a020be1f7648",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-12233",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/2f/2f0d9df3316615646dfbd994a378293dacf937050514080b5fe66af9794ae9e3.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OX}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OY}=\\mathbf{b}$ and $Z$ divides $\\overline{XY}$ in the ratio $XZ:ZY=5:2.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OZ}.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OZ}=\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{XZ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OX}=\\mathbf{a},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{XZ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OXY,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{XY} & =\\overset{\\to }{XO}+\\overset{\\to }{OY} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{OY} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $XZ:ZY=5:2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XZ}=\\frac{5}{7}\\overset{\\to }{XY}=\\frac{5}{7}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OZ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{XZ} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{7}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{7}\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
