          ":question/id": "06f1ebce-2b40-5089-bfea-ee16e90ad214",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-278290",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/36/36aeda6b6f5ce46552f55f458da60ef46a646d737c452d586389c03c47d1c9cb.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=\\mathbf{f},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=\\mathbf{g}$ and $P$ divides $\\overline{FG}$ in the ratio $FP:PG=8:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OP}.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=\\mathbf{f},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{FP}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OFG,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG} & =\\overset{\\to }{FO}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{f}+\\mathbf{g} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{g}-\\mathbf{f}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $FP:PG=8:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{FP}=\\frac{8}{13}\\overset{\\to }{FG}=\\frac{8}{13}(\\mathbf{g}-\\mathbf{f}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{f}+\\frac{8}{13}(\\mathbf{g}-\\mathbf{f}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}\\mathbf{f}+\\frac{8}{13}\\mathbf{g}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
