          ":question/problem": "![](images/2a/2a9cacfc6787e60229076c4abd2854709d51ac718c8d519256a61dbe92852b05.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=\\mathbf{g},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=\\mathbf{h},$ and $J$ divides $\\overline{GH}$ in the ratio $GJ:JH=6:7.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{g}$ and $\\mathbf{h}.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{g}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{h}$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OG}+\\overset{\\to }{GJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=\\mathbf{g},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{GJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OGH,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{GH} & =\\overset{\\to }{GO}+\\overset{\\to }{OH} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OG}+\\overset{\\to }{OH} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{g}+\\mathbf{h} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{h}-\\mathbf{g}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $GJ:JH=6:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{GJ}=\\frac{6}{13}\\overset{\\to }{GH}=\\frac{6}{13}(\\mathbf{h}-\\mathbf{g}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OG}+\\overset{\\to }{GJ} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{g}+\\frac{6}{13}(\\mathbf{h}-\\mathbf{g}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{13}\\mathbf{g}+\\frac{6}{13}\\mathbf{h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
