          ":question/problem": "![](images/36/36742531a5f9f5d77c5f7e90980120479f4142cecaf6e84937d76d938688409d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=\\mathbf{d},$ $\\overset{\\to }{ON}=\\mathbf{e},$ and $T$ divides $\\overline{MN}$ in the ratio $MT:TN=8:3.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OT}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{d}$ and $\\mathbf{e}.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OT}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{d}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{e}$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=\\mathbf{d},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{MT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OMN,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{MN} & =\\overset{\\to }{MO}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{d}+\\mathbf{e} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{e}-\\mathbf{d}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $MT:TN=8:3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{MT}=\\frac{8}{11}\\overset{\\to }{MN}=\\frac{8}{11}(\\mathbf{e}-\\mathbf{d}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{d}+\\frac{8}{11}(\\mathbf{e}-\\mathbf{d}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{11}\\mathbf{d}+\\frac{8}{11}\\mathbf{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
