          ":question/id": "037303cc-6805-57a2-b1dc-ca793be48da0",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-322577",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/de/de33644bcad663e67dc19c687dc0ef959310a50ddb83203031e66b951700510b.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=\\mathbf{u},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\mathbf{v},$ and $W$ divides $\\overline{UV}$ in the ratio $UW:WV=9:8.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OW}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OW}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{u}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{v}$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=\\mathbf{u},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{UW}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OUV,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =\\overset{\\to }{UO}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{v}-\\mathbf{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $UW:WV=9:8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{UW}=\\frac{9}{17}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=\\frac{9}{17}(\\mathbf{v}-\\mathbf{u}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OW} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{9}{17}(\\mathbf{v}-\\mathbf{u}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{17}\\mathbf{u}+\\frac{9}{17}\\mathbf{v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
