          ":question/id": "a5b0550e-551b-56de-8b66-92bcfdb0028f",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-322578",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/84/84ba52159416b3b420daa1ebd82dccac2411aee420201b9b9604937995d9553c.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OS}=\\mathbf{s},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\mathbf{t},$ and $L$ divides $\\overline{ST}$ in the ratio $SL:LT=11:4.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OL}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{s}$ and $\\mathbf{t}.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OL}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{s}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{t}$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OL}=\\overset{\\to }{OS}+\\overset{\\to }{SL}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OS}=\\mathbf{s},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{SL}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OST,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST} & =\\overset{\\to }{SO}+\\overset{\\to }{OT} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OS}+\\overset{\\to }{OT} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{s}+\\mathbf{t} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{t}-\\mathbf{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $SL:LT=11:4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{SL}=\\frac{11}{15}\\overset{\\to }{ST}=\\frac{11}{15}(\\mathbf{t}-\\mathbf{s}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OL} & =\\overset{\\to }{OS}+\\overset{\\to }{SL} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{s}+\\frac{11}{15}(\\mathbf{t}-\\mathbf{s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}\\mathbf{s}+\\frac{11}{15}\\mathbf{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
