          ":question/problem": "![](images/76/76ddb750ca447fd7f73f2481ecd46bb53eba12e392e81e8b64c2c23589e11694.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OK}=\\mathbf{k},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OZ}=\\mathbf{z},$ and $Y$ divides $\\overline{KZ}$ in the ratio $KY:YZ=10:7.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OY}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{k}$ and $\\mathbf{z}.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OY}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{k}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{z}$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OY}=\\overset{\\to }{OK}+\\overset{\\to }{KY}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OK}=\\mathbf{k},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{KY}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OKZ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{KZ} & =\\overset{\\to }{KO}+\\overset{\\to }{OZ} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OK}+\\overset{\\to }{OZ} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{k}+\\mathbf{z} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{z}-\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $KY:YZ=10:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{KY}=\\frac{10}{17}\\overset{\\to }{KZ}=\\frac{10}{17}(\\mathbf{z}-\\mathbf{k}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OY} & =\\overset{\\to }{OK}+\\overset{\\to }{KY} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{k}+\\frac{10}{17}(\\mathbf{z}-\\mathbf{k}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{17}\\mathbf{k}+\\frac{10}{17}\\mathbf{z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
