          ":question/problem": "![](images/d0/d0e71a97dc559536c25b63fda50805875d4651166a9442ae0d3d081704edebb2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OQ}=\\mathbf{q},$ and $N$ divides $\\overline{AQ}$ in the ratio $AN:NQ=12:7.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{ON}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{q}.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{ON}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{a}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{q}$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{ON}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AN}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AN}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAQ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{q} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{q}-\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AN:NQ=12:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AN}=\\frac{12}{19}\\overset{\\to }{AQ}=\\frac{12}{19}(\\mathbf{q}-\\mathbf{a}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ON} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AN} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{12}{19}(\\mathbf{q}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{19}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{12}{19}\\mathbf{q}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
