          ":question/problem": "![](images/1d/1deea2da05b0d12c7e9afbb12f0340bdbfef18ff37dc49c506929028bfeb67c4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OL}=\\mathbf{l},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\mathbf{p},$ and $Q$ divides $\\overline{LP}$ in the ratio $LQ:QP=7:9.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OQ}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{l}$ and $\\mathbf{p}.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OQ}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{l}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{p}$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OQ}=\\overset{\\to }{OL}+\\overset{\\to }{LQ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OL}=\\mathbf{l},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{LQ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OLP,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LP} & =\\overset{\\to }{LO}+\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OL}+\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{l}+\\mathbf{p} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{p}-\\mathbf{l}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $LQ:QP=7:9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{LQ}=\\frac{7}{16}\\overset{\\to }{LP}=\\frac{7}{16}(\\mathbf{p}-\\mathbf{l}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OL}+\\overset{\\to }{LQ} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{l}+\\frac{7}{16}(\\mathbf{p}-\\mathbf{l}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}\\mathbf{l}+\\frac{7}{16}\\mathbf{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186329678,
