          ":question/problem": "![](images/65/6560a7f05ae95638cbfe902dfa022b2d8de6b07c6e1e6f85051ccf87b92ec338.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=\\mathbf{h},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OI}=\\mathbf{i}$ and $J$ divides $\\overline{HI}$ in the ratio $HJ:JI=5:3.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=\\mathbf{h},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OHI,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HI} & =\\overset{\\to }{HO}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{h}+\\mathbf{i} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $HJ:JI=5:3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{HJ}=\\frac{5}{8}\\overset{\\to }{HI}=\\frac{5}{8}(\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{h}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{5}{8}(\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{h}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\mathbf{h}+\\frac{5}{8}\\mathbf{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
