          ":question/problem": "![](images/ba/ba82c6b68026b0f4339c1e4fa01c4b1aa1b7aee74b74176f81bba1c0e1de259f.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=\\mathbf{r},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OS}=\\mathbf{s}$ and $V$ divides $\\overline{RS}$ in the ratio $RV:VS=6:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OV}.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RV}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=\\mathbf{r},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{RV}.$\n\nFirst, from $△ORS,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS} & =\\overset{\\to }{RO}+\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{s}-\\mathbf{r}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $RV:VS=6:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RV}=\\frac{6}{11}\\overset{\\to }{RS}=\\frac{6}{11}(\\mathbf{s}-\\mathbf{r}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OV} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RV} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{r}+\\frac{6}{11}(\\mathbf{s}-\\mathbf{r}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{11}\\mathbf{r}+\\frac{6}{11}\\mathbf{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
