          ":question/problem": "![](images/52/52e25ccc5b59b3eecd914c5b141e443475a5de58299404528d27f1fc85db97ea.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $T$ divides $\\overline{AB}$ in the ratio $AT:TB=3:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OT}.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AT:TB=3:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AT}=\\frac{3}{8}\\overset{\\to }{AB}=\\frac{3}{8}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{8}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{8}\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
