          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
          },
          ":question/id": "2e2f6d0e-fbd4-52a2-bc5a-47ead1dbf4b7",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-322579",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/eb/eb43aa9d35e08f19fff74f030fc5246428b83f7bce907a890a3b8dfa62571dc2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OC}=\\mathbf{c},$ $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=\\mathbf{r},$ and $X$ divides $\\overline{CR}$ in the ratio $CX:XR=6:11.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OX}$ via the vectors $\\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{r}.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OX}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\mathbf{c}+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\mathbf{r}$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OX}=\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{CX}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OC}=\\mathbf{c},$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{CX}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OCR,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CR} & =\\overset{\\to }{CO}+\\overset{\\to }{OR} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{OR} \\\\  & =-\\mathbf{c}+\\mathbf{r} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{r}-\\mathbf{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $CX:XR=6:11,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CX}=\\frac{6}{17}\\overset{\\to }{CR}=\\frac{6}{17}(\\mathbf{r}-\\mathbf{c}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OX} & =\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{CX} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{c}+\\frac{6}{17}(\\mathbf{r}-\\mathbf{c}) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{17}\\mathbf{c}+\\frac{6}{17}\\mathbf{r}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186734987,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
