          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
          },
          ":question/id": "369223e9-a114-52d3-a76b-95525ee905fd",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/7d/7d75f291dcbcfa92bd92108934a7a536b6cd9924fa338b9d0f904413db778754.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $W$ lies on the segment $TF$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OT}=h$ and $\\overrightarrow{OF}=k$. The lengths satisfy $TW:WF=2:11$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OW}$ in terms of $h$ and $k$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OW}=$ {{field-1}} $h+$ {{field-2}} $k$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OT}=h\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OF}=k .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $T$ through $O$ to $F$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{TF}=\\overrightarrow{TO}+\\overrightarrow{OF}=-h+k.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $TW:WF=2:11$ gives $13$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{TW}=\\frac{2}{13}\\overrightarrow{TF}=\\frac{2}{13}(-h+k).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to T\\to W$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OW}&=\\overrightarrow{OT}+\\overrightarrow{TW}\\\\&=h+\\frac{2}{13}(-h+k)\\\\&=\\frac{11}{13}h+\\frac{2}{13}k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186735294,
