          },
          ":question/id": "5fb609a4-bafd-5754-94aa-e8f02e85d14b",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/e0/e06141dfdf949b6ea66cd5445a9d781436484bab4b1bdd2c7707bc02d6a06925.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $K$ lies on the segment $HQ$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OH}=e$ and $\\overrightarrow{OQ}=p$. The lengths satisfy $HK:KQ=9:5$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OK}$ in terms of $e$ and $p$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OK}=$ {{field-1}} $e+$ {{field-2}} $p$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OH}=e\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OQ}=p .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $H$ through $O$ to $Q$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{HQ}=\\overrightarrow{HO}+\\overrightarrow{OQ}=-e+p.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $HK:KQ=9:5$ gives $14$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{HK}=\\frac{9}{14}\\overrightarrow{HQ}=\\frac{9}{14}(-e+p).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to H\\to K$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OK}&=\\overrightarrow{OH}+\\overrightarrow{HK}\\\\&=e+\\frac{9}{14}(-e+p)\\\\&=\\frac{5}{14}e+\\frac{9}{14}p.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
