          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
          },
          ":question/id": "71218ce8-fcd7-5d9f-bfd2-75ec715e50ca",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/bc/bc3fc32b2c42ef44040a85395dc5795f85b9f2bf4c8e2b27df717bc9f3d51302.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $A$ lies on the segment $EV$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OE}=u$ and $\\overrightarrow{OV}=f$. The lengths satisfy $EA:AV=1:1$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ in terms of $u$ and $f$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OA}=$ {{field-1}} $u+$ {{field-2}} $f$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OE}=u\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OV}=f .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $E$ through $O$ to $V$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{EV}=\\overrightarrow{EO}+\\overrightarrow{OV}=-u+f.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $EA:AV=1:1$ gives $2$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{EA}=\\frac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{EV}=\\frac{1}{2}(-u+f).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to E\\to A$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OA}&=\\overrightarrow{OE}+\\overrightarrow{EA}\\\\&=u+\\frac{1}{2}(-u+f)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}u+\\frac{1}{2}f.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186735301,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/choices": [
                {
                  ":answer/id": "1341f010-6241-5fb1-aace-698406cf545d",
                  ":answer/type": {
                    ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                  },
                  ":answer/value": "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{1}{7}f+\\frac{6}{7}p",
                  ":db/id": 17592186735288
                },
                {
                  ":answer/id": "6bbc02f4-15c7-51ad-90e1-d2da7608ef6b",
                  ":answer/type": {
                    ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                  },
                  ":answer/value": "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{1}{4}f+\\frac{3}{4}p",
                  ":db/id": 17592186735296
                },
                {
                  ":answer/id": "7652cd98-5ae1-59d0-bc24-ba50c0def3e1",
                  ":answer/type": {
                    ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                  },
                  ":answer/value": "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{3}{4}f+\\frac{1}{4}p",
                  ":db/id": 17592186735299
                },
                {
                  ":answer/id": "c6824edb-6742-5231-a843-b9dc1c67e2a2",
                  ":answer/type": {
                    ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                  },
                  ":answer/value": "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{6}{7}f+\\frac{1}{7}p",
                  ":db/id": 17592186735307
                },
                {
                  ":answer/id": "fde94c3d-a081-5b40-bf18-6eba01284c55",
                  ":answer/type": {
                    ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                  },
                  ":answer/value": "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{1}{2}f+\\frac{1}{2}p",
                  ":db/id": 17592186735314
                }
              ],
              ":answer-field/correct": {
                ":answer/id": "c6824edb-6742-5231-a843-b9dc1c67e2a2",
                ":answer/type": {
                  ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                },
                ":answer/value": "\\overrightarrow{OU}=\\frac{6}{7}f+\\frac{1}{7}p",
                ":db/id": 17592186735307
              },
              ":answer-field/id": "84b23273-71dc-5752-85cc-3b72aa48c017",
              ":answer-field/key": "selection",
              ":answer-field/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer-field.type/radio"
              },
              ":db/id": 17592186735300
            }
          ],
          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
          },
          ":question/id": "86175cf5-30b4-50d0-9d04-18d042560a85",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/2f/2fcd54763ecfbdaf53ccccd7a5751a9c9f478db7403c8ee53cbb3b09d3e5e051.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $U$ lies on the segment $KC$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OK}=f$ and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=p$. The lengths satisfy $KU:UC=1:6$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OU}$ in terms of $f$ and $p$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OK}=f\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OC}=p .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $K$ through $O$ to $C$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{KC}=\\overrightarrow{KO}+\\overrightarrow{OC}=-f+p.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $KU:UC=1:6$ gives $7$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{KU}=\\frac{1}{7}\\overrightarrow{KC}=\\frac{1}{7}(-f+p).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to K\\to U$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OU}&=\\overrightarrow{OK}+\\overrightarrow{KU}\\\\&=f+\\frac{1}{7}(-f+p)\\\\&=\\frac{6}{7}f+\\frac{1}{7}p.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        }
      ],
      ":knowledge-point/title": "Expressing a Vector That Satisfies a Ratio in Terms of Known Vectors"
    },
    "17592186096701": {
      ":db/id": 17592186096701,
      ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
        ":db/id": 17592186096495,
        ":question/id": "839ed5f5-165f-5de5-aba1-551ac605475f",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "e-5212",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the picture below.\n\n![](images/f2/f2518c2e998e7c7f551548a4cc7283720a66428ea8fa9872494a81cc3848ba9e.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c} = \\lambda  \\mathbf{a} + 2 \\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that when two known vectors are not parallel, a linear combination of them is unique. So, once we rewrite $\\mathbf c$ in terms of $\\mathbf a$ and $\\mathbf b,$ we can match coefficients to determine the unknown scalar.\n\nTo find $\\lambda,$ we want to match the expression\n$$\n\\mathbf{c} = \\lambda  \\mathbf{a} + 2 \\mathbf{b} .\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $2 \\mathbf{b} .$ So, we first draw the vector $2 \\mathbf{b}$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/ea/ea517ac4ca8e0bcf7ba48f23e66f100323d5485f1221219aacfbea9148f4a1af.png)\n\nNote that in $△ O D C$, we have:\n\n- $D C = 2 | \\mathbf{a} |$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{D C}$ and $\\mathbf a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overrightarrow{D C} = 2 \\mathbf{a} .$\n\nAdditionally,\n$$\n\\begin{array}{cc}\\mathbf{c} &  = \\overrightarrow{O D} + \\overrightarrow{D C} \\\\  &  = 2 \\mathbf{b} + 2 \\mathbf{a} .\\end{array}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c} = \\lambda  \\mathbf{a} + 2 \\mathbf{b} = 2 \\mathbf{b} + 2 \\mathbf{a} .$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a} \\nparallel \\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf a,$ we get:\n$$\n\\lambda=2\n$$"
      },
