          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-321299",
          ":question/problem": "![](images/6f/6fe3721ff3ab63e75be934c79b03d4ca601513c2e08b987a0bafd94c74856e90.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $\\mathbf{c}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda \\mathbf{b}$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $\\mathbf{a}.$ So, we begin with the vector $\\mathbf{a},$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](images/9c/9c8d67718152bc1bc9569213369580b6fc6f5bc1fe0c63b637f14c9f659dfe27.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=\\frac{2}{3}|\\mathbf{b}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=\\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{c} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda \\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{2}{3}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{b},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\lambda =\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186302311,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/choices": [
                {
                  ":answer/id": "f77b9a46-e79c-5237-bc79-ede8d68a69b6",
                  ":answer/type": {
                    ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                  },
                  ":answer/value": "2",
                  ":db/id": 17592186301182
                }
              ],
              ":answer-field/correct": {
                ":answer/id": "f77b9a46-e79c-5237-bc79-ede8d68a69b6",
                ":answer/type": {
                  ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                },
                ":answer/value": "2",
                ":db/id": 17592186301182
              },
              ":answer-field/id": "5972d618-ef56-509e-bacd-8caba67f5cfd",
              ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
              ":answer-field/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer-field.type/blank"
