          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"
          },
          ":question/id": "764ad590-6274-55b2-ba3a-f46517308ea0",
          ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/02/021a6f546c13d39b564182ed59eb6acb028eb78a8cedb806c7af9ca33a534779.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, ending at $A$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &=1\\,(5, 0)=(5, 0). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{AC} &=(0, -4).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/5c/5cd541ffafe7d74e419825c6f244e4583f1bb8040c46f2fd2975f4032078865c.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(0, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-4}{-4}=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{AC}=\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=1$."
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186735389,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/choices": [
                {
                  ":answer/id": "6599b991-1558-5ba1-b641-353caddf656a",
                  ":answer/type": {
                    ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                  },
                  ":answer/value": "3",
                  ":db/id": 17592186735382
                }
              ],
              ":answer-field/correct": {
                ":answer/id": "6599b991-1558-5ba1-b641-353caddf656a",
                ":answer/type": {
                  ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
                },
                ":answer/value": "3",
