          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"
          },
          ":question/id": "a5fd80a9-ebec-5fea-9956-08afd7118da5",
          ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/9b/9bc9cd6832996ed599ed7c5fca9ed2c8c6f2772106024f6c1ea0b09c79f3c4b7.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\\,(0, 2)=(0, 2). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{BC} &=(-6, 0).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b9/b98f2bf570523f9f4ae296b3e321820c6feb3a351fdab7186b60ff60646d11f6.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-2, 0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-6}{-2}=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{BC}=3\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OB}+\\overrightarrow{BC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{b}+3\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=3$."
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186735391,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/choices": [
