          ":question/id": "dd31157d-3178-5399-ab80-97eed38cdf4f",
          ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/6e/6e475a645584c44f974d631bbdbf4e065ad611f1bc4e365a1441adeba95e462a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\\,(-5, 0)=(-5, 0). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{BC} &=(0, -7).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ea/ea6e3ab1951e7aebfcce1c3ed7a26696966ba3bb0a7bb8be86e888e062e3e94e.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(0, -2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-7}{-2}=\\frac{7}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{BC}=\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OB}+\\overrightarrow{BC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{7}{2}$."
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186735397,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
