          },
          ":question/id": "c2ac4d7e-a633-5182-a775-d21ede953b8c",
          ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/df/dfb02e1d9202130f955625a46621b81e8fdb9ff6c7f66e183577eb13e2ad2775.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{5}{2}\\,(-2, 3)=\\left(-5, \\frac{15}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(-7, 7).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ae/ae434599433e3432485a0a5d2d410c20d7a13e0d16847cb5a6c7f281587e03b2.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(-4, 4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-7}{-4}=\\frac{7}{4} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{7}{4}$."
        }
      ],
      ":knowledge-point/title": "Finding a Scalar Factor in a Linear Combination"
